# Cell from playpick: mode=battleground map=conquest spec=priest:shadow
# style=wander view=1280x800 save=fresh.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl and every .play under playtest/plans/ first. `wander`
# has only ever been run on a battleground once before (2026-09-28-19.play,
# escort/priest:discipline, carried): it died once at fightTime=54 -- much
# later than any `good`-style death (9-16s, a beeline straight into the
# enemy cluster at the spawn) but earlier than `flee`/`dodge`'s "never dies
# at all" shape -- then respawned, drifted `Out of range` of both carts, and
# contributed nothing for the rest of the match. direction.md's #7 called
# that one pull, one map, wants a second `wander` pull on the *other* map
# before it counts as a shape rather than a coincidence.
#
# This is that second pull, on conquest (The Three Cairns) instead of escort,
# and on shadow instead of discipline -- also the first `wander` run with a
# `save=fresh` profile rather than `carried` (moot per #273, carried already
# behaves as fresh). Conquest specifically has its own separate thread on
# this line: two different `good`-style specs (druid:balance, then
# druid:restoration) both died at fightTime~9s on this exact map, read as
# "conquest's own opening geometry punishes closing distance in the first
# ~9 seconds" rather than a kit problem. `wander` doesn't beeline at
# anything on purpose, so this pull also tests whether that geometry catches
# a body that isn't aiming at it.
open
targets
shot front

tap battleground
targets
shot bg-menu

tap map:conquest
targets
shot conquest-picked

tap class:priest:shadow
shot class-picked

tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot pulled
state
targets

play wander 90
shot mid1
state
bill
says

wait 5
play wander 90
shot mid2
state
bill

wait 5
play wander 90
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
